      "text": "# Transactional Inventory Ledger: Design & Reference Implementation\n\n## 1. Design Overview\n\nThis system implements a **double-entry style inventory ledger** where every stock movement is recorded as an immutable transaction. The design ensures:\n\n- **Idempotency**: Duplicate requests produce no side effects.\n- **Concurrency Safety**: Optimistic locking with version checks prevents lost updates.\n- **Audit Invariants**: Balance = sum of all movements; no negative stock without explicit allowance.\n- **Migrations**: Versioned schema changes with rollback support.\n- **Tested**: Comprehensive test suite covering edge cases.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Schema Design\n\n```sql\n-- Schema version tracking\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS schema_version (\n    version INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n    applied_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (datetime('now')),\n    description TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n\n-- Products: the inventory items\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS products (\n    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,           -- UUID or SKU\n    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n    sku TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,\n    created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (datetime('now')),\n    updated_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (datetime('now')),\n    version INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,  -- Optimistic locking\n    allow_negative INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0  -- Allow negative stock?\n);\n\n-- Inventory Ledger: immutable transaction log\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS inventory_ledger (\n    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    transaction_id TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,  -- Idempotency key\n    product_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES products(id),\n    quantity_change INTEGER NOT NULL,     -- Positive = inbound, Negative = outbound\n    balance_after INTEGER NOT NULL,       -- Denormalized for fast reads\n    reason TEXT NOT NULL,                 -- 'purchase', 'sale', 'adjustment', 'return', etc.\n    reference TEXT,                       -- External reference (order ID, PO number)\n    created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (datetime('now')),\n    created_by TEXT NOT NULL,             -- User/system identifier\n    metadata TEXT                         -- JSON blob for extra context\n);\n\n-- Indexes for performance\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_ledger_product ON inventory_ledger(product_id);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_ledger_transaction ON inventory_ledger(transaction_id);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_ledger_created ON inventory_ledger(created_at);\n\n-- Current stock view (materialized via trigger or computed)\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS inventory_balance (\n    product_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES products(id),\n    quantity INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n    last_updated TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (datetime('now')),\n    version INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1  -- Optimistic locking\n);\n\n-- Audit log for schema changes and critical operations\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS audit_log (\n    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    action TEXT NOT NULL,           -- 'schema_migration', 'stock_adjustment', etc.\n    entity_type TEXT NOT NULL,      -- 'product', 'ledger', 'schema'\n    entity_id TEXT,\n    old_value TEXT,                 -- JSON\n    new_value TEXT,                 -- JSON\n    performed_by TEXT NOT NULL,\n    performed_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (datetime('now')),\n    ip_address TEXT,\n    user_agent TEXT\n);\n```\n\n### Key Design Decisions\n\n| Aspect | Decision | Rationale |\n|--------|----------|-----------|\n| **Ledger Immutability** | No UPDATE/DELETE on `inventory_ledger` | Full audit trail; corrections via compensating transactions |\n| **Idempotency** | `transaction_id` UNIQUE constraint | Duplicate inserts fail gracefully; client retries are safe |\n| **Concurrency** | Optimistic locking via `version` column | SQLite doesn't support row-level locks; version check prevents lost updates |\n| **Balance Tracking** | Dual: `balance_after` in ledger + `inventory_balance` table | Fast reads from balance table; ledger is source of truth |\n| **Negative Stock** | Configurable per product | Some businesses allow overselling; others don't |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Python Reference Implementation\n\n```python\n\"\"\"\nTransactional Inventory Ledger with SQLite backend.\n\nFeatures:\n- Idempotent transactions via unique transaction_id\n- Optimistic concurrency control via version columns\n- Audit invariants enforced at application and DB level\n- Versioned migrations with rollback support\n- Comprehensive test suite\n\"\"\"\n\nimport sqlite3\nimport uuid\nimport json\nimport threading\nfrom contextlib import contextmanager\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom enum import Enum\nfrom typing import Optional, List, Dict, Any, Tuple\nimport logging\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# Exceptions\n# =============================================================================\n\nclass InventoryError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base exception for",
